I thought it might be fun to have a list of one-line spoilers and
good game strategies sort of like the "true" fortunes.  Anybody
have anything to add or change in this list?

some spoilers below

The adventurer who fights and runs away lives to fight another day!
A picky eater will go hungry in the dungeon.
Kick a door to get it out of the way.
Why do they call them grid bugs?
Use the armor that you find.
Throw your darts and arrows liberally!
Blindness and hallucination eventually wear off.
If it's interesting... well, it's not.
Go back upstairs if you're in trouble.
You are what you eat.
Books are very heavy.
Traps are good for getting monsters.
If you can't escape, run in circles.  Run around boulders.
Never eat very rotten food.
If you're fast then you should hit and retreat.
If you beat up a chest, you'll eventually break it open.
If you beat up a sink, you'll find what went down the drain.
If you beat up a throne, you'll see what it's made of.
If you beat up an altar, you'll be in big trouble.
It'll disagree with you if it's yellow, green, or violet.
Don't get surrounded by rothes or orcs.  Hallways are okay.
Disarm goblins by letting them throw their only weapon at you.
If you are a Samauri or a Priest, you are very good at kicking.
What could a guard on patrol be guarding?
Things happen when you drink from a fountain or dip things in it.
Things happen when you sit on a throne.
Things happen when you offer a fresh sacrifice at an altar.
The Gnomish Mines are too hard if you're weak.  Go the other way.
With a shopkeeper guarding the door, shops are a good place to hide.
It's nice to feel like someone is helping you when your whole game is cursed.
Money is for spending.  Don't be a miser like Croesus.
Don't kill your pet.  It makes everybody angry.
Most molds, jellys, oozes, and puddings are good for you.  Eat them.
Animals are blinded by bright lights.
Every good thief wants a tourist's credit card.
Iron rusts.  Bronze, silver, gold, and mithril don't.
Isn't it confusing when your hands begin to glow red?
If you steal, you will get caught.  If your pet steals...
When your numbers are down, do something that makes you feel good!
Unless you feel healthy, don't eat kobolds, snakes, or things that sting.
Pets fear curses.
Animals are frightened by reflections, laughter, and Elbereth.
Water dilutes potions and washes out scrolls.
Some rings burn more calories than others.
Magic fountains, like holy water, can lift a curse.
It is cruel to force your pet into a trap.
Strange things happen when you drink from a sink.
A floating eye can give you a new point of view.
Unicorn horns can make everything seem SO boring.
Some adventurers drink healing potions only when they're not hurt.
It takes a hard gem or a powerful wand to beat a dusty finger.
What does a baby cockatrice look like?
Doing a lot of searching is good for your wisdom.
Lepraucans would be at a loss if they couldn't rob you.
If you're afraid to drink it, throw it away.
When you're confused, grease can be less than enchanting.
A dagger named Sting is like a two handed sword named Orcist.
It might be wise to let your pet step on a polymorph trap.
Djinis do not grant three wishes.
Blindfolds are useful if you have a strange mental acuity.
Remember who your god is.
Altars reveal the divine nature of things.
Shaping up all those piles of junk can actually add life to your game.
Poison can improve darts, so darts are pretty useful.
A pickaxe can recover items from a petrified creature.
Naming something rustproof doesn't actually make it rustproof.
The limbs of a lizard never stiffen or age.
Consider yourself lucky if you can kick a gray stone.
Potions can be mixed by dipping.
Shopkeepers are paralyzed by fear when it comes to invisible adventurers.
Beware: nymphs steal the things that you are most attached to.
Wishing for more wishes might not be what you bargained for.
A Wizard's athame never dulls.
If you can count, you won't need a fedora to recognize value.
A smoky potion can be as empty as a magic lamp.
If you lose a ring down a sink, watch carefully.
A broken mirror is seven years of bad luck.
There are musical instruments with powerful magic.
Stop reading when it vibrates suddenly.
You can ire your god by sacrificing your pet.
Rust monsters eat almost anything.  Really.
Good things happen if you donate enough to your temple.
Avoid energy vortices unless your health currently feels amplified.
If you think nothing can bring you down, you haven't tried a sink.
A fog cloud can be a very safe place.
Eating a wraith corpse will never make you rise through the ceiling.


David


